## Insight 5

Movies on Netflix showcase a wide range of durations, from a few minutes to over four hours, indicating that audiences are comfortable with varying lengths. In contrast, TV shows reveal a distinct trend, with producers favoring mini-series of one season. Audiences seem to prefer these shorter formats, typically comprising 1 to 3 episodes, as they provide enough time to convey the intended story. While longer TV shows, particularly sitcoms, can engage viewers over multiple seasons, creating a stable and long-term audience base, mini-series offer a concise storytelling approach that appeals to modern viewers.

